-- ccc29-xxvii-a-interpretation-penalty.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART XXVII Summary Convictions:
-- section 785 (definitions: "In this Part"), section 786 (application of the Part; the 12-month limitation) and
-- section 787 (the general penalty; imprisonment in default). Layer 1: the law, objectively; no point of view.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. The French equivalents in
-- parentheses after a defined term are quoted with the line they sit on and are not encoded.
--
-- HOW AN ANSWER READS (the rule of 2026-10-29, applied exactly; see NOTES.md "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING"):
--   JUST TRUE   the facts bring the case within the rule, on the text's own words;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "unless", "except", "where",
--               "when", a flat negative, a period it fixes itself);
--   NOTHING     not covered: the text includes without closing the list, is silent, points outside its sources, or limits a grant
--               in its own wording and the case is outside the limit. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`; every branch that answers
-- "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.

§ `Part XXVII -- Summary Convictions (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-46)`

§§ `Section 785 -- Interpretation: definitions ("In this Part")`

-- 785 In this Part, ...: the definitions below apply in Part XXVII, that is, in sections 785 to 840 (Part XXVIII begins at section 841).
-- src:16687 | Definitions
-- src:16688 | 785 In this Part,
@ref Criminal Code s 785 lead-in (src:16687-16688)
GIVEN `the section number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 785 the definitions apply` MEANS
    IF `the section number` AT LEAST 785 AND `the section number` AT MOST 840
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this Part,"

-- clerk of the appeal court includes a local clerk of the appeal court.
-- src:16689 | clerk of the appeal court includes a local clerk of the appeal court; (greffier de la cour d’appel)
@ref Criminal Code s 785 "clerk of the appeal court" (src:16689)
GIVEN `the person is the clerk of the appeal court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a local clerk of the appeal court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 785 clerk of the appeal court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is the clerk of the appeal court` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is a local clerk of the appeal court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "clerk of the appeal court includes a local clerk of the appeal court"

-- informant means a person who lays an information.
-- src:16690 | informant means a person who lays an information; (dénonciateur)
@ref Criminal Code s 785 "informant" (src:16690)
GIVEN `the person lays an information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 785 informant` MEANS
    IF `the person lays an information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "informant means a person who lays an information"

-- information includes (a) a count in an information, and (b) a complaint in respect of which a justice is authorized ... to make an order.
-- src:16691 | information includes
-- src:16692 | (a) a count in an information, and
-- src:16693 | (b) a complaint in respect of which a justice is authorized by an Act of Parliament or an enactment made thereunder to make an order; (dénonciation)
@ref Criminal Code s 785 "information" to s 785 "information" (b) (src:16691-16693)
GIVEN `it is an information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a count in an information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a complaint in respect of which a justice is authorized by an Act of Parliament or an enactment made thereunder to make an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 785 information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an information` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is a count in an information` THEN JUST TRUE   -- paragraph (a)
        IF `it is a complaint in respect of which a justice is authorized by an Act of Parliament or an enactment made thereunder to make an order` THEN JUST TRUE   -- paragraph (b)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "information includes"

-- order means any order, including an order for the payment of money.
-- src:16694 | order means any order, including an order for the payment of money; (ordonnance)
@ref Criminal Code s 785 "order" (src:16694)
GIVEN `it is an order, including an order for the payment of money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 785 order` MEANS
    IF `it is an order, including an order for the payment of money`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "order means any order, including an order for the payment of money"

-- proceedings means (a) proceedings in respect of offences declared ... punishable on summary conviction, and (b) proceedings where a justice is authorized ... to make an order.
-- src:16695 | proceedings means
-- src:16696 | (a) proceedings in respect of offences that are declared by an Act of Parliament or an enactment made thereunder to be punishable on summary conviction, and
-- src:16697 | (b) proceedings where a justice is authorized by an Act of Parliament or an enactment made thereunder to make an order; (procédures)
@ref Criminal Code s 785 "proceedings" to s 785 "proceedings" (b) (src:16695-16697)
GIVEN `they are proceedings in respect of an offence that is declared by an Act of Parliament or an enactment made thereunder to be punishable on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are proceedings where a justice is authorized by an Act of Parliament or an enactment made thereunder to make an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 785 proceedings` MEANS
    IF `they are proceedings in respect of an offence that is declared by an Act of Parliament or an enactment made thereunder to be punishable on summary conviction`   -- paragraph (a)
       OR `they are proceedings where a justice is authorized by an Act of Parliament or an enactment made thereunder to make an order`   -- paragraph (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "proceedings means"

-- prosecutor means the Attorney General or, where the Attorney General does not intervene, the informant, and includes counsel or an agent acting on behalf of either of them.
-- src:16698 | prosecutor means the Attorney General or, where the Attorney General does not intervene, the informant, and includes counsel or an agent acting on behalf of either of them; (poursuivant)
@ref Criminal Code s 785 "prosecutor" (src:16698)
DECLARE `s 785 prosecutor: who the person is` IS ONE OF
    `s 785 prosecutor: the Attorney General`
    `s 785 prosecutor: the informant, where the Attorney General does not intervene`
    `s 785 prosecutor: the informant, where the Attorney General intervenes`
    `s 785 prosecutor: counsel or an agent acting on behalf of the Attorney General or of the informant`
    `s 785 prosecutor: a person who is none of those`

@ref Criminal Code s 785 "prosecutor" (src:16698)
GIVEN who IS A `s 785 prosecutor: who the person is`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 785 prosecutor` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `s 785 prosecutor: the Attorney General` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 785 prosecutor: the informant, where the Attorney General does not intervene` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 785 prosecutor: the informant, where the Attorney General intervenes` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the Attorney General does not intervene"
    WHEN `s 785 prosecutor: counsel or an agent acting on behalf of the Attorney General or of the informant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 785 prosecutor: a person who is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prosecutor means the Attorney General"

-- sentence includes (a) a declaration made under 199(3), (b) an order made under 109(1) or 110(1), 320.24, 730(1) or 737(2.1) or (3) or 738, 739, 742.1 or 742.3,
-- (c) a disposition made under 731 or 732 or 732.2(3) or (5), 742.4(3) or 742.6(9), (d) an order under 16(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, (e) an order under 94(1) of the Cannabis Act.
-- src:16699 | sentence includes
-- src:16700 | (a) a declaration made under subsection 199(3),
-- src:16701 | (b) an order made under subsection 109(1) or 110(1), section 320.24, subsection 730(1) or 737(2.1) or (3) or section 738, 739, 742.1 or 742.3,
-- src:16702 | (c) a disposition made under section 731 or 732 or subsection 732.2(3) or (5), 742.4(3) or 742.6(9),
-- src:16703 | (d) an order made under subsection 16(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, and
-- src:16704 | (e) an order made under subsection 94(1) of the Cannabis Act; (sentence, peine ou condamnation)
@ref Criminal Code s 785 "sentence" to s 785 "sentence" (e) (src:16699-16704)
GIVEN `the provision under which it was made` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `it is an order made under subsection 16(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an order made under subsection 94(1) of the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 785 sentence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 199
           AND `the provision under which it was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3)"
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a): a declaration made under subsection 199(3)
        IF (    `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 109
             OR `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 110 )
           AND `the provision under which it was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)"
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b): subsection 109(1) or 110(1)
        IF `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 320.24
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b): section 320.24
        IF `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 730
           AND `the provision under which it was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)"
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b): subsection 730(1)
        IF `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 737
           AND (    `the provision under which it was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2.1)"
                 OR `the provision under which it was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3)" )
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b): subsection 737(2.1) or (3)
        IF `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 738
           OR `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 739
           OR `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 742.1
           OR `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 742.3
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b): section 738, 739, 742.1 or 742.3
        IF `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 731
           OR `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 732
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (c): section 731 or 732
        IF (    (    `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 732.2
                  AND (    `the provision under which it was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3)"
                        OR `the provision under which it was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(5)" ) )
             OR (    `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 742.4
                 AND `the provision under which it was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3)" )
             OR (    `the provision under which it was made`'s `section` EQUALS 742.6
                 AND `the provision under which it was made`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(9)" ) )
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (c): subsection 732.2(3) or (5), 742.4(3) or 742.6(9)
        IF `it is an order made under subsection 16(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (d)
        IF `it is an order made under subsection 94(1) of the Cannabis Act` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (e)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "sentence includes"

-- summary conviction court means a person who has jurisdiction in the territorial division where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen and who (a), (b) or (c).
-- src:16705 | summary conviction court means a person who has jurisdiction in the territorial division where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen and who
-- src:16706 | (a) is given jurisdiction over the proceedings by the enactment under which the proceedings are taken,
-- src:16707 | (b) is a justice or provincial court judge, where the enactment under which the proceedings are taken does not expressly give jurisdiction to any person or class of persons, or
-- src:16708 | (c) is a provincial court judge, where the enactment under which the proceedings are taken gives jurisdiction in respect thereof to two or more justices; (cour des poursuites sommaires)
@ref Criminal Code s 785 "summary conviction court" to s 785 "summary conviction court" (c) (src:16705-16708)
GIVEN `the person has jurisdiction in the territorial division where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is given jurisdiction over the proceedings by the enactment under which the proceedings are taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a justice or a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment under which the proceedings are taken expressly gives jurisdiction to any person or class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment under which the proceedings are taken gives jurisdiction in respect of them to two or more justices` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 785 summary conviction court` MEANS
    IF `the person has jurisdiction in the territorial division where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen`
       AND (    `the person is given jurisdiction over the proceedings by the enactment under which the proceedings are taken`   -- paragraph (a)
             OR (    `the person is a justice or a provincial court judge`   -- paragraph (b)
                 AND NOT `the enactment under which the proceedings are taken expressly gives jurisdiction to any person or class of persons` )
             OR (    `the person is a provincial court judge`   -- paragraph (c)
                 AND `the enactment under which the proceedings are taken gives jurisdiction in respect of them to two or more justices` ) )
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "summary conviction court means a person who has jurisdiction in the territorial division"

-- trial includes the hearing of a complaint.
-- src:16709 | trial includes the hearing of a complaint. (procès ou instruction)
@ref Criminal Code s 785 "trial" (src:16709)
GIVEN `it is a trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the hearing of a complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 785 trial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a trial` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is the hearing of a complaint` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "trial includes the hearing of a complaint"

§§ `Section 786 -- Application of the Part; limitation`

-- 786(1) Except where otherwise provided by law, this Part applies to proceedings as defined in this Part.
-- src:16710 | Application of Part
-- src:16711 | 786 (1) Except where otherwise provided by law, this Part applies to proceedings as defined in this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 786(1) (src:16710-16711)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings as defined in section 785, by s 785 proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the law otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 786(1) this Part applies to the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the law otherwise provides` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except where otherwise provided by law"
        IF `the proceedings are proceedings as defined in section 785, by s 785 proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this Part applies to proceedings as defined in this Part"

-- 786(2) No proceedings shall be instituted more than 12 months after the time when the subject matter of the proceedings arose, unless the prosecutor and the defendant so agree.
-- src:16712 | Limitation
-- src:16713 | (2) No proceedings shall be instituted more than 12 months after the time when the subject matter of the proceedings arose, unless the prosecutor and the defendant so agree.
@ref Criminal Code s 786(2) (src:16712-16713)
GIVEN `the date the subject matter of the proceedings arose` IS A DATE
      `the date the proceedings were instituted` IS A DATE
      `the prosecutor and the defendant so agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 786(2) the proceedings are barred because they were instituted more than 12 months after the subject matter arose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the prosecutor and the defendant so agree` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the prosecutor and the defendant so agree"
        IF `the date the proceedings were instituted` AT MOST (`s 786(2) the day on which the 12 months end` `the date the subject matter of the proceedings arose`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No proceedings shall be instituted more than 12 months after"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The 12 months run from the day the subject matter arose to the same day of the month 12 months later (the last day of the month where the month has no such day) (fork F-786-2: the other reading rolls 29 February forward to 1 March).
@ref Criminal Code s 786(2) (src:16712-16713)
GIVEN `the date the subject matter of the proceedings arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 786(2) the day on which the 12 months end` MEANS
    `add months` `the date the subject matter of the proceedings arose` 12

§§ `Section 787 -- Punishment`

-- 787(1) Unless otherwise provided by law, every person who is convicted of an offence punishable on summary conviction is liable to a fine of not more than $5,000 or to a term of imprisonment of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
-- src:16716 | General penalty
-- src:16717 | 787 (1) Unless otherwise provided by law, every person who is convicted of an offence punishable on summary conviction is liable to a fine of not more than $5,000 or to a term of imprisonment of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref Criminal Code s 787(1) (src:16716-16717)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 787(1) the general penalty as stated in section 787(1)` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`), `no imprisonment is stated`, (`a fine of` 5000), `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 787(1) (src:16716-16717)
GIVEN `the offence is punishable on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 787(1) the general penalty applies to the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is punishable on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every person who is convicted of an offence punishable on summary conviction"
        IF `the law otherwise provides` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise provided by law"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 787(1) (src:16716-16717)
GIVEN `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 787(1) the fine is not more than $5,000` MEANS
    IF `the fine in dollars` AT MOST 5000
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine of not more than $5,000"

-- A term of imprisonment is asked in whole months: "two years less a day" is 23 months and the last month's days but one, so a term of 23 whole months is inside it and a term of 24 whole months is not (fork F-787-1: a term in days is not converted).
@ref Criminal Code s 787(1) (src:16716-16717)
GIVEN `the term of imprisonment in whole months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 787(1) the term of imprisonment is not more than two years less a day` MEANS
    IF `the term of imprisonment in whole months` AT MOST 23
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a term of imprisonment of not more than two years less a day"

-- 787(2) If the imposition of a fine or the making of an order for the payment of money is authorized by law, but the law does not provide that imprisonment may be imposed in default of payment ..., the court may order that in default ... the defendant shall be imprisoned for a term of not more than two years less a day.
-- src:16718 | Imprisonment in default if not otherwise specified
-- src:16719 | (2) If the imposition of a fine or the making of an order for the payment of money is authorized by law, but the law does not provide that imprisonment may be imposed in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order, the court may order that in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order, as the case may be, the defendant shall be imprisoned for a term of not more than two years less a day.
@ref Criminal Code s 787(2) (src:16718-16719)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "If ... is authorized by law, but the law does not provide" (fork F-787-2)
GIVEN `the imposition of a fine or the making of an order for the payment of money is authorized by law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law provides that imprisonment may be imposed in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 787(2) the court may order imprisonment in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order` MEANS
    IF `the imposition of a fine or the making of an order for the payment of money is authorized by law`
       AND NOT `the law provides that imprisonment may be imposed in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the imposition of a fine or the making of an order for the payment of money is authorized by law, but the law does not provide that imprisonment may be imposed in default"

@ref Criminal Code s 787(2) (src:16718-16719)
-- @name-test: outside the sweep: a value (a term of imprisonment), not a grant that can answer JUST FALSE
GIVETH AN Imprisonment
`s 787(2) the longest term of imprisonment the court may order in default` MEANS
    `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`
